<DocsLayout title="Google ADK guide | Agent-Gantry" description="Integrate Agent-Gantry with Google ADK: per-turn tool selection through before_model_callback, ADK tool confirmation, readable tool errors and session context.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Framework guide</p>
  <h1>Google ADK</h1>
  <p class="lead">Agent-Gantry plugs into the Agent Development Kit's own mechanisms: <code>before_model_callback</code> picks each model request's tools, <code>require_confirmation</code> handles human approval, and the <code>ToolContext</code> carries your session state. Failures come back to the model as <code>&#123;"error": ...&#125;</code> responses instead of ending the run.</p>
  <p><a class="pill" href="/Agent-Gantry/docs/frameworks/google-adk/advanced/">Advanced Google ADK usage →</a></p>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`uv add "agent-gantry[google-adk]"   # google-adk >= 2.6.1`} />

  <h2>Basic page: per-turn tools</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="python" title="Per-turn tool selection" code={`import asyncio

from google.adk.runners import InMemoryRunner
from google.genai import types
from agent_gantry import AgentGantry
from agent_gantry.google_adk import GoogleADKAdapter

gantry = AgentGantry()

@gantry.register(examples=["where is my order", "has order 4471 shipped"])
def get_order_status(order_id: str) -> str:
    """Return the current shipping status for an order."""
    return "in_transit"

async def main():
    await gantry.sync()
    agent = GoogleADKAdapter(gantry).agent(model="gemini-2.5-flash", name="support", limit=5)
    runner = InMemoryRunner(agent=agent, app_name="support")
    session = await runner.session_service.create_session(app_name="support", user_id="u")
    message = types.Content(role="user", parts=[types.Part(text="Has order 4471 shipped?")])
    async for event in runner.run_async(user_id="u", session_id=session.id, new_message=message):
        if event.is_final_response():
            print(event.content.parts[0].text)

asyncio.run(main())`} />
  <p>For an agent you build yourself, pass <code>before_model_callback=adapter.before_model_callback(limit=5)</code>. Tools the agent already has stay available; Gantry adds its selection each turn.</p>

  <h2>What the model sees when a tool fails</h2>
  <p>A failed call returns <code>&#123;"error": "&lt;type&gt;: &lt;message&gt;"&#125;</code> as the function response, capped at 2,000 characters, which is how ADK tells a model a tool failed. An exception would end the run instead.</p>
  <div class="callout"><strong>Redact or opt out:</strong> <code>GoogleADKAdapter(gantry, error_formatter=redact)</code> rewrites the text the model sees; <code>error_mode="raise"</code> lets <code>ToolExecutionError</code> propagate instead.</div>

  <h2>Reading session state from a Gantry tool</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="python" code={`from agent_gantry.google_adk import current_tool_context

@gantry.register
def get_balance(account: str) -> str:
    """Fetch an account balance for the signed-in user."""
    ctx = current_tool_context()   # ADK ToolContext, or None outside a run
    return bank.balance(ctx.state["user_id"], account)`} />
